---
layout: base
title: Maps
description: "Interactive maps of Ahvantir and the city of Aru'Mas."
permalink: /map/
---

{# Layout: the frame runs full width with the locations underneath it, rather
   than a column down the right.

   The city image is 4962x3508, so it is landscape by a wide margin. A side
   column takes its width away from the one axis it needs most, and squeezes 50
   locations across 10 groups into a single long scroll. Underneath, the frame
   keeps the full width and the list gets horizontal room to lay out in columns.

   The ids and class names map.js and map-editor.js attach to are unchanged:
   #map-canvas, #map-toolbar, #map-select, #map-toggles, #map-status,
   #map-marker-list, #map-sidebar-hint, .map-page and .map-sidebar. #}

<div class="map-page" id="map-page">

  {# Restoring these: the first pass at this layout dropped the page-header and
     the sidebar's h2, which left /map/ shipping with no heading elements at all
     and no statement of what the page is or how to use it. #}
  <div class="map-head">
    <h1 class="map-head__title">Maps</h1>
    <p class="map-head__lead">Hover a marker for a summary, or open its article from the list below.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="map-toolbar" id="map-toolbar" hidden>
    <label class="map-switch">
      <span class="map-switch__label">Map</span>
      <select id="map-select" class="map-switch__select" aria-label="Choose a map"></select>
    </label>
  </div>

  <div class="map-stage">
    <div class="map-canvas" id="map-canvas" aria-label="Interactive map of Ahvantir"></div>
    <div class="map-status" id="map-status" role="status">
      <div class="map-status__inner">
        <span class="map-status__icon" aria-hidden="true">🗺</span>
        <p class="map-status__title">Loading maps…</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="map-browser">
    <div class="map-browser__bar">
      <label class="map-search">
        <span class="sr-only">Search locations</span>
        <input type="search" id="map-search" class="map-search__input"
               placeholder="Search locations…" autocomplete="off">
      </label>
      <div class="map-toggles" id="map-toggles" role="group" aria-label="Filter layers"></div>
      <button type="button" class="map-browser__collapse" id="map-list-toggle"
              aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="map-sidebar">
        <span class="map-browser__collapse-text">Hide list</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <aside class="map-sidebar" id="map-sidebar" aria-labelledby="map-sidebar-title">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="map-sidebar-title">Locations on this map</h2>
      {# Filtering changes the list silently for a screen reader: the visible
         count is obvious to a sighted user and invisible to everyone else. #}
      <p class="sr-only" id="map-filter-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="map-sidebar__hint" id="map-sidebar-hint">Select a map to see what has been marked on it.</p>
      <div class="map-marker-list" id="map-marker-list"></div>
    </aside>
  </div>

</div>

{% block scripts %}
{# Leaflet and Geoman both come from jsdelivr: it is the only CDN the
   Content-Security-Policy in base.njk allows for scripts and styles. #}
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha384-sHL9NAb7lN7rfvG5lfHpm643Xkcjzp4jFvuavGOndn6pjVqS6ny56CAt3nsEVT4H"
      crossorigin="anonymous">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha384-cxOPjt7s7Iz04uaHJceBmS+qpjv2JkIHNVcuOrM+YHwZOmJGBXI00mdUXEq65HTH"
        crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2.108.1/dist/umd/supabase.min.js" integrity="sha384-UQ9Ztz63gzT2JZCuDRkNXV8RP/gXxdPUuM9LKlz2BzqGx9xFYNAK8yAEgbfZHs7P" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/auth-storage.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/player.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/map-coords.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/map.js"></script>
{# Inert for visitors: it checks is_dm() first and only then fetches the
   drawing library, so a reader never downloads the editor's 290 KB. #}
<script src="/assets/js/map-editor.js"></script>
{# A signed-in player's own pins and notes. Private to them, enforced by RLS;
   inert for anonymous visitors, and it needs no drawing library. #}
<script src="/assets/js/map-player-notes.js"></script>
{% endblock %}
